# Cryptogenic Organizing Pneumonia

- **Definition** - subacute flu-like illness of unknown cause with migratory lesions, often mistakened as pneumonia
- **Etiology of COP:**
  - Idiopathic
  - Secondary to CTD (esp. polymyositis and dermatomyositis)
  - Medications
  - Underlying malignancy (may be related to immune-mediated myositis)
- **HRCT findings in COP** - patchy, and ocassionally migratory lesions:
  - Subpleural opacities associated w/ GGOs
  - Peribronchiolar or perilobar involvement also present
  - Reversed halo sign (rim of subpleural sparing)
- **Histopathology of COP:**
  - Patchy regions of organiszing pneumonia evident by granulation tissues
  - Often in with surrounding inflammation that may affect alveolar wall
- **Mx** - corticosteroids (may be required up to 6 mo as relapse rate high)
